Let me look at the function signature more carefully:

```
{
  "name": "execute",
  "description": "Send an API request (HTTP / GraphQL / MCP) — the side-effecting action.\n\nTwo ways to call it:\n\n1. **Inline (one step — use this for most calls):** pass the request content\n   directly via `request`, e.g.\n   `execute(request={\"protocol\": \"rest\", \"method\": \"GET\", \"url\": \"/v3/users\",\n   \"headers\": {...}, \"body\": {...}})`. It is sent immediately; the request is\n   also auto-saved as a `request` entity in the workspace for audit/reuse.\n",
  "parameters": {
    "properties": {
      "mode": ...,
      "request": {
        "description": "inline request content (REST: `{method, url, headers?, body?, protocol: \"rest\"}`; ..."
      },
      "target": ...
    }
  }
}
```

OK so the format I need is:
```
execute(request={"protocol": "rest", "method": "GET", "url": "/openapi.json"})
```

Let me try this properly.

